&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a dynamic and results-driven Network Partner Manager / Network Business Development professional to lead the Fireblocks Network in APAC. This role is crucial in driving the growth strategy of the Fireblocks Network by fostering strong relationships with key industry players, accelerating adoption of Off-Exchange Settlement, and expanding our Network footprint across the region.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relationship Management&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and nurture strong relationships with exchanges, fiat partners, on/off ramps, and other key network providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary point of contact for existing and potential partners, ensuring seamless communication and collaboration with the Business Lead, Product and R&amp;amp;D.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Development&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the adoption of Off-Exchange Settlement among clients and venues in APAC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand our Network footprint by identifying and onboarding new strategic partner&amp;nbsp;Banks, Exchanges, Custodians, and On/Off Ramp providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct market research and analysis to identify emerging Network opportunities and trends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market Representation&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Fireblocks Network at industry events, conferences, and client meetings across the APAC region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion the Fireblocks Network and its value proposition to potential partners and clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide valuable market insights and feedback to the global team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with internal teams (product, engineering, marketing, and sales) to ensure alignment and support for regional initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years of experience in the cryptocurrency, stablecoin, or payments industry in a customer-facing role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the APAC crypto and digital asset landscape, including key industry players, exchanges, and payment providers for on/off ramps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of building and maintaining strong business&amp;nbsp;relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, presentation, and interpersonal skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and as part of&amp;nbsp;a global team.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;span id=&quot;m_-7851985116603247750gmail-sources&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel frequently throughout the APAC region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ideally located in Singapore, other major financial centres in APAC will be considered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English. Additional regional languages are a bonus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fireblocks&#39; mission is to enable every business to easily and securely access digital assets and cryptocurrencies. In order to do that, we strongly believe&amp;nbsp;our workforce should be as diverse as our clients, and this is why we&amp;nbsp;embrace diversity and inclusion in all its forms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.fireblocks.com/candidate-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Please see our candidate privacy policy here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The world of digital assets is accelerating in speed, magnitude, and complexity, opening the door to new ways for leveraging the blockchain. Fireblocks’ platform and network provide the simplest and most secure way for companies to work with digital assets and it trusted by some of the largest financial institutions, banks, globally-recognized brands, and Web3 companies in the world, including BNY Mellon, BNP Paribas, ANZ Bank, Revolut, and thousands more.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly experienced policy professional with a passion for blockchain technology and digital identity to join our Legal Team as we navigate a complex and evolving global regulatory environment.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Director of Policy - North America, you will be part of the Policy sub-group within the Fireblocks Legal Department.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be expected to establish, cultivate, and maintain relationships with key policymakers, legislators, and regulators in the US and Canada, in order to advance Fireblocks’ core mission of enabling all businesses to safely and securely interact with digital assets.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have an additional responsibility to work with Fireblocks’ Identity and Compliance Product teams to inform and enable the development of identity capabilities within our platform that reduce friction in the access to and transfers of crypto-assets, financial instruments, and payment funds.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To be successful in this role, you will need to work closely with the in-house regulatory team, product, and sales to understand strategic priorities and craft effective messages and delivery strategies in different geographic regions.&amp;nbsp; You will also be engaging directly with clients from time to time to help them navigate - and collaborate on shaping - digital asset regulation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is anticipated that you will be required to engage and manage local experts to maximize the impact of your work.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base for this role is the US, with a strong preference for a NYC or Washington DC-based candidate.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage directly with policymakers to shape public dialogue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and lead public policy strategy for Fireblocks products and businesses, including working with cross-functional teams to formulate our policy positions and strategies to support our global business objectives and drive favorable policy and regulatory outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver regulatory analysis and, if needed, public sector engagement, to support our emerging identity products suite.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic advice on the direction of US policy to the leadership team to inform our product and business strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage a network of key senior stakeholder and influencer relationships to help shape a positive policy and regulatory environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct policy projects on a host of issues affecting the industry, e.g. custody of digital assets, trade and settlement of RWAs, issuance and intermediation of stablecoins, staking and lending, DeFi connectivity, privacy, and any other issue impacting Fireblocks’ ability or its customer&#39;s ability to offer services in North America .&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Requirements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience working on policy issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on public policy issues in the technology industry, in particular as an advisor and partner to business teams in product development, go-to-market, and other business areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with or for regulated industries, business strategy consultancies, or the technology industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with international teams and a variety of stakeholders&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead and evaluate issues independently in a fast-paced environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent personal, political, analytical, and communications skills and high attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable product experience would be considered a positive differentiator&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable digital identity experience would be considered a positive differentiator&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For employees hired to work remotely from New York, or from our NYC HQ, Fireblocks is required by law to include a reasonable estimate of the compensation range for this role. This range is specific to New York City and takes into consideration a wide range of factors that are reviewed when making a hiring decision, such as years of experience, skills, and other business needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is not typical for a candidate to be hired at or near the top of the pay range and each compensation decision is dependent on each individual case. A reasonable base salary range estimate for this position is $175,000 - $240,000. The base salary is one component of the total compensation package, which for some roles may include a target bonus, a very competitive equity grant, and very generous benefits.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While we believe competitive compensation is a critical aspect of your decision to join us, we do hope you also spend time considering why our mission and culture are right for you. We are creating something transformational here, and we hope you are as excited about the future as we are.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
