&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The world of digital assets is accelerating in speed, magnitude, and complexity, opening the door to new ways for leveraging the blockchain. Fireblocks’ platform and network provide the simplest and most secure way for companies to work with digital assets and it trusted by some of the largest financial institutions, banks, globally-recognized brands, and Web3 companies in the world, including BNY Mellon, BNP Paribas, ANZ Bank, Revolut, and thousands more.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re building our Blockchain Engineering presence in our New York City office to spearhead blockchain technology initiatives and establish foundational infrastructure for our expanding product suite. This is a unique opportunity to shape blockchain engineering practices at a market-leading company while working on cutting-edge solutions that power institutional digital asset operations.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;As a Blockchain Engineer, you will be instrumental in the research and integration of blockchain technologies into the Fireblocks platform. Your responsibilities will include collaborating closely with foundations and developers to gain a deep understanding of blockchain protocols and on-chain projects. This knowledge will then be applied to implement new features within the Fireblocks platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be focusing equally on external protocol integration patterns and internal wallet infrastructure. This role serves as a technical bridge between raw on-chain integrated capabilities and the valuable wallet features delivered to customers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This role will report into our Senior Director, Wallet Technology.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our team works in a hybrid model with three days in our NYC office.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
